          equipment: 'Standard 32-card French pack, score sheet with +/- columns.',
          dealing: 'Deal 6 cards each. Center cards (widow) are dealt face-up or face-down depending on player count (e.g., 2 face-up for 5 players).',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'As declarer: Win your bid total in trick points + Roem. As defender: Stop the declarer. Overall: Win two rounds to be safe; avoid losing two rounds.',
          gameplay: '1. **Auction**: Players bid point totals or special contracts (Misère, Zwabber). 2. **Exchange**: High bidder swaps cards with the center widow. 3. **Trump**: High bidder names the trump suit. 4. **Tricks**: 6 tricks played. **Must Follow Suit** rule is modified: you may trump even if you could follow suit. 5. **Roem**: Combinations (sequences/sets) announced at the first trick.',
          keyRules: [
            'Jass Trump Ranking: Jack (20), 9 (14), Ace (11), 10 (10), King (4), Queen (3), 8 (0), 7 (0).',
            'Jack of Trumps can be withheld when trumps are led (Undertrumpping/Withholding).',
            "Opponents can 'Counter-Roem' to cancel the declarer's bonus points.",
            "Two '+' marks = Safe (exit game). Two '-' marks = Loser (buy drinks).",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Only bid for Declarer if you hold the Jack or Nine of trumps. The center cards are a gamble; don't rely on them to fix a void.",
          intermediate: "The 'Trump Over' Maneuver: Use the rule allowing you to trump when you have the suit to steal high-point Tens or Aces from opponents early in the hand.",
          advanced: 'Roem Calculation: Precisely calculate your sequence values before bidding. If an opponent is likely to have a higher sequence, your bid may fail because your Roem will be cancelled.',
          tips: [
            'Wait for the right hand to bid Boonaak (all tricks) only when you control both the trumps and high side-suit cards.',
            'In Misère (avoiding all tricks), use the withholding rule to dump your high trumps safely.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
