          deckDescription: 'One standard 32-card deck: eight ranks (seven through ace) in each of four French suits. No jokers; used for Boonaken (Belote-family game) where the jack and nine of trump are the two highest cards and marriages score.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Trump is determined by the turned card or bid; follow suit when able. The jack (20 points) and nine (14 points) of trump outrank all other trumps in Boonaken.',
          rankDescription: 'Eight ranks per suit: seven, eight, nine, ten, jack, queen, king, ace. In trump: jack highest, then nine, ace, ten, king, queen, eight, seven. In plain suits: ace, ten, king, queen, jack, nine, eight, seven. Point values as in Belote family.',
          dealPattern: 'Cards are dealt individually or in batches of three clockwise.',
          bettingLimits: 'None',
          actions: {},
          handRankingSystem: 'None; card point values (Jack=20, 9=14, Ace=11...) determine victory in the 141-point round.',
          rankingSystem: 'Jass (Boer-Nel-Aas)',
          useTrump: true,
          notApplicableReasons: {
            drawConfig: 'All cards are distributed at the start of the deal and exchange; no draw pile exists during trick play.',
            specialCards: 'Cards follow the Jass dynamic trump ranking but do not trigger automated secondary engine actions.',
            declarationMechanism: 'Roem and bidding are performed verbally around the table; no hidden tokens are required.',
            fishingConfig: 'Boonaken is a trick-taking game and does not use a capture-from-tableau fishing mechanic.',
            shedding: 'The goal is to meet a point total rather than being the first to empty the hand.',
          },
